{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>לחכם לב</b> — that the wisdom is in his heart." "<b>יקרא נבון</b> — that he understands what he did not learn." "<b>ומתק שפתים</b> — the meaning: and a man will learn from the sweetness of lips, then he will add learning." "<b>והמתק</b> — an allusion to sweet wisdom, as in the phrase: and sweeter than honey."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {3 "Citation appears to be Judges 14:18 (ומתוק מדבש) or 1 Samuel 14:29 (ראיתי כי מתוק הדבש); Ibn Ezra cites the phrase in abbreviated form without a full verse reference."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:13.625767387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}